<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maharero</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1820–<a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Kamaherero</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maharero, also called Kamaherero, was a Herero leader in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> who freed the Herero from the domination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oorlam">Oorlam</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaners">Afrikaners</a> in a war that began in 1863. Based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okahandja">Okahandja</a>, he became the most powerful Herero chief, and in 1885 he signed a protection treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. He died in 1890 and was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-maharero">Samuel Maharero</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maharero.jpg" alt="Maharero" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Opperhoofman_Maharero.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
